.TH COUNT_FILES 1 "October 2026" "count-files 2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
count_files \- count files in a directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B count_files
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
count_files is a Bash script that counts files, directories,
and symbolic links in a specified directory.Version 2.0 also displays the largest file in the selected directory

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-r
Search through subdirectories recursively.

.TP
.B \-e EXTENSION
Count files with the specified extension.

.SH EXAMPLES
Count files in the default /etc directory:
.PP
count_files

.PP
Count files recursively:
.PP
count_files \-r

.PP
Count .conf files:
.PP
count_files \-e conf

